            <ArticleTitle>[An abscess of the piriforme muscle as a rare cause of sciatic neuralgia. A case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rare cause of sciatic neuralgia, an abscess in the sciatic foramen, is presented. The most common causes of sciatic neuralgia are discussed. We analyse correlations between symptoms found in a young woman and anatomical structures of the supra- and infrapiriforme foramen and their neighborhood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
